WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.684
JAMIE: China's Foreign Ministry pushed
back on Amodei's call — not just the

00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:07.369
JAMIE: general slowdown idea, but
specifically his suggestion that the
U.S. should curb

00:00:07.369 --> 00:00:11.054
JAMIE: China's AI development. Reported
September fourteenth. And they tied it
to the

00:00:11.054 --> 00:00:14.738
JAMIE: broader global debate.

00:00:14.838 --> 00:00:18.256
ALEX: So now the slowdown conversation
has three layers. Amodei saying the
industry

00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:21.675
ALEX: should slow. Trump saying the U.S.
shouldn't. And Beijing saying nobody
gets

00:00:21.675 --> 00:00:25.093
ALEX: to tell China what to do.

00:00:25.193 --> 00:00:28.761
RUFUS: Which means if there were ever a
path to a coordinated global

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:32.328
RUFUS: pause — the kind that would
actually address the safety concern in

00:00:32.328 --> 00:00:35.896
RUFUS: a meaningful way — it has now
been loudly rejected by both

00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:39.463
RUFUS: superpowers, from opposite
directions.
